---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
        <title>SnapSpace · Privacy Policy</title>
        <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
        <style>
            html,
            body {
                overflow: auto !important;
                height: auto !important;
            }
        </style>
    </head>
    <body class="privacy-page">
        <div class="privacy-container">
            <header class="privacy-header">
                <a href="/" class="privacy-back">← Back</a>
                <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            </header>
            <main class="privacy-content">
                <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: 14 August 2026</p>

                <h2>1. Controller</h2>
                <p>
                    The controller responsible for data processing within the
                    meaning of the EU General Data Protection Regulation
                    (Datenschutz-Grundverordnung, DSGVO) is:
                </p>
                <p>
                    Jonas Ludorf · Email: <a
                        class="contact-mail footer-link"
                        href="#"></a>
                </p>
                <p>
                    No data protection officer has been appointed, as the legal
                    requirements for a mandatory appointment are not met.
                </p>

                <h2>2. What Data We Process</h2>
                <p>
                    When you use SnapSpace on your Meta Quest headset and in
                    this web viewer, the following data is processed:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Raw Sensor Data:</strong> Spatial and camera frame
                        data captured by your headset's sensors to map your physical
                        environment. Camera frames may show your surroundings and,
                        if present, other people.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Point Cloud &amp; Mesh Data:</strong> 3D spatial representations
                        (scans) of the specific spaces you choose to capture within
                        the app, including derived data such as camera poses and reconstructed
                        meshes.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Account Data:</strong> If you create an account: your
                        email address, a display name you choose, a securely hashed
                        password, your account role and the creation timestamp.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Sharing Data:</strong> Which captures belong to or
                        have been shared with your account, and share links you create.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Server Log Data:</strong> Each request to this website
                        is logged by our hosting providers for operational and security
                        purposes. This includes your IP address, date and time, the
                        requested URL, HTTP status, referrer and browser/user agent
                        string.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    We kindly ask that you do not scan highly private or
                    sensitive spaces, and that you do not scan other people
                    without their knowledge and agreement. Try to only share
                    spaces you feel comfortable sharing.
                </p>

                <h2>3. Purposes and Legal Bases</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Providing the app and web viewer</strong> (capturing,
                        processing, storing and displaying your scans; account management;
                        login; sharing) — Art. 6(1)(b) DSGVO (performance of a contract
                        / pre-contractual measures).
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Transactional emails</strong> such as account confirmation
                        and password reset — Art. 6(1)(b) DSGVO.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong
                            >Server logs, IT security, abuse and error
                            detection, stability</strong
                        > — Art. 6(1)(f) DSGVO (legitimate interest in operating a
                        secure and functional service).
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong
                            >Public display of scans during the test phase</strong
                        > — Art. 6(1)(a) DSGVO (consent), which you give by choosing
                        to upload a scan while this notice is in effect. You can withdraw
                        this at any time by requesting deletion (see section 8); withdrawal
                        does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before
                        the withdrawal.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Providing account and scan data is not legally required, but
                    without it the app cannot be used. We do not carry out
                    automated decision-making or profiling within the meaning of
                    Art. 22 DSGVO.
                </p>

                <h2>4. Public Visibility During the Test Phase</h2>
                <p>
                    All point clouds generated via the headset are automatically
                    synced to this companion web viewer. During the test phase,
                    these scans as well as the associated sensor data may be
                    visible to anyone visiting this site. Please treat
                    everything you upload as potentially public.
                </p>

                <h2>5. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
                <p>
                    This website does not use advertising cookies, analytics, or
                    any third-party tracking technologies. We do not embed
                    social media plugins, fonts loaded from external servers, or
                    advertising networks.
                </p>
                <p>
                    We only use storage that is strictly necessary to provide
                    the service you requested (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG / ePrivacy
                    exemption), which is why no cookie consent banner is shown:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Authentication cookies</strong> (set by Supabase,
                        names beginning with <code>sb-</code>): keep you logged
                        in and protect your session. They are only set once you
                        log in and are removed when you log out.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Session storage</strong> (<code
                            >ss_pending_confirm_email</code
                        >): temporarily remembers the email address you just
                        registered with, so the confirmation page can show it.
                        It is stored in your browser only and cleared when you
                        close the tab.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h2>6. Hosting, Processors and Third-Party Services</h2>
                <p>
                    We do not sell your data and we do not share it with third
                    parties for their own purposes. We do, however, rely on the
                    following service providers, who process data on our behalf
                    under data processing agreements pursuant to Art. 28 DSGVO:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Vercel Inc.</strong> (340 S Lemon Ave #4133, Walnut,
                        CA 91789, USA) — hosting and delivery of this website and
                        its serverless functions. For security and operational purposes,
                        technical data such as IP addresses, request metadata and
                        browser information is processed by Vercel. Vercel is based
                        in the USA; transfers are safeguarded by EU Standard Contractual
                        Clauses and Vercel's certification under the EU–U.S. Data
                        Privacy Framework. See the <a
                            href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="footer-link">Vercel Privacy Policy</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> (101 Townsend St., San Francisco,
                        CA 94107, USA) — authoritative DNS for the domain <code
                            >snapspace.cloud</code
                        >. When your device looks up our domain, Cloudflare
                        processes the DNS query and the IP address of the
                        resolver making it. Our DNS records are <strong
                            >not</strong
                        > proxied through Cloudflare, so Cloudflare does not receive,
                        terminate or inspect the content of your requests to this
                        website. Transfers to the USA are safeguarded by EU Standard
                        Contractual Clauses. See the <a
                            href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="footer-link">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Supabase Inc.</strong> (970 Toa Payoh North, Singapore
                        / Supabase Pte. Ltd.) — authentication, account database and
                        transactional emails. Our Supabase project is hosted in the
                        EU (Frankfurt/Ireland region). See the <a
                            href="https://supabase.com/privacy"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="footer-link">Supabase Privacy Policy</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>STRATO GmbH</strong> (Otto-Ostrowski-Straße 7, 10249
                        Berlin, Germany) — the server that receives, processes and
                        stores your scans and raw sensor data (<code
                            >api.snapspace.cloud</code
                        >). Data is stored on servers located in Germany. See
                        the <a
                            href="https://www.strato.de/datenschutz/"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            class="footer-link">STRATO Privacy Policy</a
                        >.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    This website is built with <a
                        href="https://astro.build/"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        class="footer-link">Astro</a
                    >, an open-source framework. Astro runs on our own
                    infrastructure and does not itself collect or transmit any
                    data about you.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Please note that the SnapSpace headset app runs on Meta
                    Quest hardware. Your use of the headset and the Meta
                    platform is additionally subject to the <a
                        href="https://www.meta.com/legal/privacy-policy/"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        class="footer-link">Meta Privacy Policy</a
                    >, over which we have no control.
                </p>

                <h2>7. Retention Periods</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Scans, raw sensor data and derived data:</strong
                        > stored until you request their deletion or your account
                        is deleted.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Account data:</strong> stored for as long as your
                        account exists; deleted after an account deletion request.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Server log data:</strong> retained only as long as
                        necessary for security and troubleshooting, and deleted or
                        anonymised thereafter in accordance with our providers' retention
                        policies.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Longer retention only occurs where we are legally required
                    to keep specific data.
                </p>

                <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
                <p>Under the DSGVO you have the right to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        request <strong>access</strong> to the personal data we hold
                        about you (Art. 15);
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        request <strong>rectification</strong> of inaccurate data
                        (Art. 16);
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        request <strong>erasure</strong> of your data (Art. 17);
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        request <strong>restriction</strong> of processing (Art. 18);
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        receive your data in a portable format (<strong
                            >data portability</strong
                        >, Art. 20);
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>object</strong> to processing based on legitimate
                        interests (Art. 21);
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>withdraw consent</strong> at any time with effect
                        for the future (Art. 7(3)).
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    We provide this process for all users, irrespective of their
                    region, and we do not charge any fees for fulfilling data
                    deletion requests. If you request the deletion of your data,
                    we will promptly remove your specific point cloud scans from
                    the web viewer and securely delete the associated raw sensor
                    data from our servers. We will fulfil all deletion requests
                    unless we are strictly required by law to retain specific
                    data.
                </p>
                <p>
                    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
                    protection supervisory authority, in particular in the EU
                    member state of your habitual residence, place of work, or
                    the place of the alleged infringement (Art. 77 DSGVO).
                </p>

                <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
                <p>
                    All traffic to this website and to our API is encrypted via
                    HTTPS/TLS. Passwords are never stored in plain text. Access
                    to scans and account data is protected by row-level security
                    rules and short-lived signed URLs, and credentials for our
                    backend API are only ever used server-side and never exposed
                    to your browser.
                </p>

                <h2>10. Children</h2>
                <p>
                    SnapSpace is not directed at children under the age of 16.
                    If you become aware that a child has provided us with
                    personal data, please contact us and we will delete it.
                </p>

                <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
                <p>
                    As SnapSpace is under active development, we may update this
                    privacy policy to reflect changes to the service or to legal
                    requirements. The current version always applies, and the
                    date at the top of this page indicates when it was last
                    revised.
                </p>

                <h2>12. Contact</h2>
                <p>
                    If you have any questions, privacy concerns, or wish to
                    formally request access to or deletion of your data, please
                    contact me directly via: <a
                        id="contact-mail"
                        class="contact-mail footer-link"
                        href="#"></a>.
                </p>
            </main>
            <footer class="app-footer">
                <span
                    >&copy; <a
                        href="https://jonasludorf.dev"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        class="footer-link">Jonas Ludorf</a
                    ></span
                >
                <span class="footer-sep">|</span>
                <a href="https://jonasludorf.dev/legal/" class="footer-link"
                    >Legal Note</a
                >
            </footer>
        </div>
        <script>
            const u = "contact";
            const d = "snapspace.cloud";
            document.querySelectorAll(".contact-mail").forEach((el) => {
                if (el instanceof HTMLAnchorElement) {
                    el.href = "mailto:" + u + "@" + d;
                    el.textContent = u + "@" + d;
                }
            });

            const backLink = document.querySelector(".privacy-back");
            if (backLink) {
                try {
                    const ref = document.referrer
                        ? new URL(document.referrer)
                        : null;
                    if (ref && ref.origin === location.origin) {
                        const path = ref.pathname.replace(/\/+$/, "") || "/";
                        if (path === "/viewer")
                            backLink.setAttribute("href", "/viewer");
                        else if (path === "/")
                            backLink.setAttribute("href", "/");
                    }
                } catch {}
            }
        </script>
    </body>
</html>
